'''{{ill|Dewa no Shikinai-sha Ichiran|de|Dewa no Shikinai-sha Ichiran|ja|出羽国の式内社一覧|zh|出羽国の式内社一覧}}''' (Dewa no Kuni no Shikinaisha Ichiran) is a list of {{ill|Shrine|de|Shrine|ja|神社|zh|神社}} – that is, the shrines recorded in the 9th and 10th volumes of the {{ill|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|de|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|ja|延喜式神名帳|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|zh|延喜式神名帳}} (“Kamimyōchō Jōge”) – in addition to those shrines designated as {{ill|Shikinai Shrines|de|Shikinai Shrines|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|zh|式内社}} and their corresponding {{ill|Candidate Shrines|de|Kandidatschreine|ja|論社|zh|論社}} that are classified as part of {{ill|Dewa Province|de|Dewa Province|ja|出羽国|zh|出羽国}}.
It also includes shrines which, although they existed at the time of the compilation of the {{ill|Engishiki|de|Engishiki|ja|延喜式|zh|延喜式}}, are not recorded in its Kamimyōchō – the so‐called “{{ill|Shikigai Shrines|de|Shikigai Shrines|ja|式外社|1=Shikigeisha|zh|式外社}}”.
--> == Shikinai Shrines (式内社) ==
In the Engishiki, a list of major Shinto shrines is recorded – 2 groups (2 shrines, both of which are {{ill|Myojin Taisha|de|Myojin Taisha|ja|Myojin Taisha|zh|Myojin Taisha}}) and 7 groups (7 minor shrines) for a total of 9 groups, 9 shrines.
