This is a '''List of Shikinaisha in Dewa Province'''. Or the list of shrines in [[Dewa Province]] which is present in the {{ill|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|ja|延喜式神名帳|12=draft}}. On this page we will also cover the {{ill|Shikigeisha|ja|式外社|1=Shikigeisha|12=draft}} of [[Dewa Province]] which are shrines that are known to have existed at that time due to other historical records, such as the [[Rikkokushi]], but for some reason were excluded from the {{ill|Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|ja|延喜式神名帳|12=draft}}. We will cover them in a separate list to avoid confusion.
== Shikinai Shrines (式内社) ==
In the Engishiki, a list of major Shinto shrines is recorded – 2 groups (2 shrines, both of which are {{ill|Myojin Taisha|de|Myojin Taisha|ja|Myojin Taisha|zh|Myojin Taisha|12=draft}}) and 7 groups (7 minor shrines) for a total of 9 groups, 9 shrines.
